# Windows, quality, masks and anomaly thresholds over a synthetic stream

## Goal

Resample a versioned synthetic temperature stream into a window, encode it
with an explicit fill policy so bad-quality samples become masked rows, score
the last observed value against the window mean with a small `defn`, and
decode the score as an inert anomaly with a threshold. The Lab convenience
`Wotex.Lab.Examples.WindowAnomaly.run/1` is shown beside the `wotex_nx`
calls it makes.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:nx, "~> 0.13.1"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`docs/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout. The data is synthetic
and labeled so; no model is trained and no accuracy is claimed.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Window layout, resampling strategies, fills, masks, quality codes, dtype limits | `wotex_nx` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Nx.Window`, `Encoder`, `Decoder`, `OutputSchema` |
| The synthetic stream, its equation, seed and glitch schedule | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.Simulators.Thermal` |
| The score `defn`, threshold and persistence baseline | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.Examples.WindowAnomaly` |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.DataSchema
alias Wotex.Lab.Examples.WindowAnomaly
alias Wotex.Lab.Simulators.Thermal
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.Nx.{Anomaly, Decoder, Encoder, Feature, Observation, OutputSchema, Row, Schema, Window}

telemetry_id = "cookbook-window-anomaly-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
```

The convenience lane: a heater step at sample 28 and a sensor glitch at 30.

```elixir
{:ok, heated} = WindowAnomaly.run(seed: 7, heater: %{28 => 4.0}, glitches: [30])
{:ok, repeated} = WindowAnomaly.run(seed: 7, heater: %{28 => 4.0}, glitches: [30])
{:ok, quiet} = WindowAnomaly.run(seed: 7)

%{
  heated: heated.anomaly,
  quiet_score: Nx.to_number(quiet.score),
  window: heated.manifest["window"],
  deterministic?: heated.anomaly == repeated.anomaly and Nx.to_number(heated.score) == Nx.to_number(repeated.score)
}
```

The same lane through the package API. The simulator records its equation
and inputs in a manifest; every sample is a synthetic Celsius value.

```elixir
simulation = Thermal.generate(seed: 7, count: 32, heater: %{28 => 4.0}, glitches: [30])
{:ok, observations} = WindowAnomaly.observations(simulation.samples)
thing_id = "urn:wotex:lab:room:simulated"

{:ok, data_schema} = DataSchema.new(%{"type" => "number", "unit" => "Cel"})

{:ok, feature} =
  Feature.new(
    name: "temperature",
    thing_id: thing_id,
    affordance_type: :property,
    affordance_name: "temperature",
    data_schema: data_schema,
    accepted_quality: [:good, :uncertain],
    missing: {:fill, 18.0}
  )

{:ok, schema} = Schema.new(features: [feature], max_rows: 64)
{:ok, window} = Window.new(start: 24_000, step: 1_000, count: 8, strategy: :latest)
{:ok, rows} = Window.resample(observations, schema, window)

{:ok, encoded} =
  Nx.with_default_backend(Nx.BinaryBackend, fn -> Encoder.encode(rows, schema) end)

{{_values}, {masks}, quality} =
  Nx.Defn.jit_apply(&Function.identity/1, [encoded], compiler: Nx.Defn.Evaluator)

%{
  equation: simulation.manifest["equation"],
  masks: Nx.to_flat_list(masks),
  quality: Nx.to_flat_list(quality),
  glitch_row: Enum.at(rows, 6).provenance["temperature"]
}
```

Score and decode: the threshold is rounded to the output dtype, and the
decoder rejects any output whose shape or dtype disagrees with the schema.

```elixir
score =
  Nx.with_default_backend(Nx.BinaryBackend, fn ->
    Nx.Defn.jit_apply(&WindowAnomaly.score/1, [encoded], compiler: Nx.Defn.Evaluator)
  end)

{:ok, score_schema} = DataSchema.new(%{"type" => "number", "minimum" => 0})

{:ok, anomaly_output} =
  OutputSchema.new(
    kind: :anomaly,
    thing_id: thing_id,
    affordance_type: :property,
    affordance_name: "temperature",
    data_schema: score_schema,
    dtype: :f32,
    threshold: 1.5,
    anomaly_rule: :at_or_above
  )

{:ok, anomaly} = Decoder.decode(score, anomaly_output, id: "anomaly-31000", produced_at: 31_000)
{Nx.to_number(score), anomaly}
```

## Deliberate breakage

Stale windows, Kelvin observations against a Celsius feature, and integers
outside an `s8` feature are refused with typed errors instead of values.

```elixir
{:error, stale} = WindowAnomaly.run(seed: 3, window_start: 1_000_000, max_age: 0)

{:ok, kelvin} =
  Observation.new(
    id: "kelvin",
    thing_id: thing_id,
    affordance_type: :property,
    affordance_name: "temperature",
    observed_at: 0,
    value: 293.15,
    unit: "K"
  )

{:ok, kelvin_row} = Row.new(0, %{"temperature" => kelvin})
{:error, kelvin_error} = Encoder.encode([kelvin_row], schema)

{:ok, integer_schema} = DataSchema.new(%{"type" => "integer"})

{:ok, count_feature} =
  Feature.new(
    name: "count",
    thing_id: thing_id,
    affordance_type: :property,
    affordance_name: "count",
    data_schema: integer_schema,
    dtype: :s8
  )

{:ok, count_schema} = Schema.new(features: [count_feature])

{:ok, big} =
  Observation.new(
    id: "big",
    thing_id: thing_id,
    affordance_type: :property,
    affordance_name: "count",
    observed_at: 0,
    value: 200
  )

{:ok, big_row} = Row.new(0, %{"count" => big})
{:error, dtype_error} = Encoder.encode([big_row], count_schema)

{:error, shape_error} =
  Decoder.decode(Nx.tensor([1.0, 2.0], type: :f32), anomaly_output, id: "bad", produced_at: 0)

{stale, kelvin_error.code, dtype_error.code, shape_error.code}
```

## Safe telemetry

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)

profiles =
  for {[:wotex, :lab, :nx, operation, :stop], _measurements, metadata} <- spans,
      do: {operation, metadata.profile}

labels_safe? = not (inspect(spans) =~ "urn:wotex") and not (inspect(spans) =~ "18.0")
{Enum.uniq(profiles), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `heater-anomalous` | The heated run scores at or above `1.5` and is `anomalous?: true` |
| `quiet-not-anomalous` | The quiet run scores below `0.5` |
| `deterministic` | The same seed and schedule give the same anomaly and score |
| `glitch-masked` | Row 6 of the window has mask `0` and quality code `2` (`:bad`) |
| `stale-window-refused` | A window past every sample yields `:no_observed_row` |
| `kelvin-refused` | Encoding fails with `:unit_conversion_required` |
| `dtype-refused` | `200` in `s8` fails with `:dtype_value_out_of_range`; a vector output is `:output_shape_mismatch` |

```elixir
%{
  "heater-anomalous" =>
    match?(%Anomaly{anomalous?: true, threshold: 1.5, rule: :at_or_above}, heated.anomaly) and
      anomaly.anomalous? and Nx.to_number(score) >= 1.5,
  "quiet-not-anomalous" => match?(%Anomaly{anomalous?: false}, quiet.anomaly) and Nx.to_number(quiet.score) < 0.5,
  "deterministic" =>
    heated.anomaly == repeated.anomaly and Nx.to_number(heated.score) == Nx.to_number(score),
  "glitch-masked" =>
    Nx.to_flat_list(masks) == [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1] and
      Nx.to_flat_list(quality) == [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0] and
      Enum.at(rows, 6).provenance["temperature"] == "sim-30",
  "stale-window-refused" => stale == :no_observed_row,
  "kelvin-refused" => kelvin_error.code == :unit_conversion_required,
  "dtype-refused" =>
    dtype_error.code == :dtype_value_out_of_range and shape_error.code == :output_shape_mismatch and
      labels_safe?
}
```

## Public seam

`nx.unit_converter` is not used here on purpose: the feature and the
observations share a unit, and a mismatch is a typed refusal. The lane
exercises `Wotex.Nx.Window` and the encoder/decoder contract of `WNX.01`.

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.03 `window-anomaly` lane (`WLB-C03`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `WNX-C01`, `WNX-C02`, `WNX-C04`.

## Replacement adapter

Replace the simulator with your own observation source by producing
`Wotex.Nx.Observation` values with the Thing id, affordance, time, unit and
quality your device reports; `Window.resample/3` and the encoder do not care
where they came from. Replace `WindowAnomaly.score/1` with any function that
accepts the `{{values}, {masks}, quality}` container and returns a scalar of
the declared dtype; keep decoding through `Decoder.decode/3` so the
threshold and schema are applied.
